{#- The art Project's room template (ticket 0348): the game's room-brief skill (urban-mystery-club, .claude/skills/room-brief,
    v1) as a Jinja2 template. Shared rules that don't depend on the room are in style/bible.md. -#}
{%- set screen = 640 -%}{#- the game's internal width (kiripix.toml [project] resolution) -#}
{%- set k = canvas_width / width -%}
{%- set adult = (52 * k) | round | int -%}
{%- set door_w = (32 * k) | round | int -%}
{%- set door_h = (64 * k) | round | int -%}
{%- set wall = (80 * k) | round | int -%}
{%- set small = width < screen -%}
{%- set sides = {"top": "set into the back wall, facing the camera", "bottom": "as a gap in the bottom edge, between two door-frame posts",
                 "left": "at the left edge of the image", "right": "at the right edge of the image", "": "where the notes say"} -%}
Use the attached image only for the camera angle and projection; ignore its content, palette and lighting.

Painterly pixel art game background{% if mood %}: {{ mood }}{% endif %}, in the style of a 16-bit JRPG {{ "side-view platformer" if view == "side" else "interior" }}. High-angle oblique view, the camera looks down at the room at about 60 degrees. Orthographic projection: no perspective, no vanishing point; parallel lines stay parallel. Not isometric: the floor is a rectangle and the back wall runs perfectly horizontal. The floor fills two thirds of the room's height; side walls are thin vertical strips. Every object, including small clutter, is drawn from the same camera as the room, its top visible.
{%- if small %} The room is a cutaway box in the middle of the frame, surrounded by plain black; no ceiling; the front wall is cut away. The room fills about {{ (100 * width / screen) | round | int }}% of the image width.{% endif %}

Scale: everything is sized for a standing adult about {{ adult }} px tall ({{ "%.2f" | format(adult / canvas_height) }} of the image height). Furniture at true scale next to that adult. A door is a little taller than an adult, about {{ door_w }} px wide and {{ door_h }} px tall. The back wall is about {{ wall }} px tall from the floor to its top edge.
{%- if exits %}

Exits:
{%- for e in exits %}
- "{{ e.name }}": {{ sides[e.side] }}, with clear floor in front for a person to stand.
{%- endfor %}
{%- endif %}
{%- if notes %}

{{ notes }}
{%- endif %}

The floor's open walking space reads on a {{ (tile * k) | round | int }} px grid: clear floor in runs of whole tiles; all furniture sits square to the walls.

{{ bible }}
